{"id":"5abc65f95514f629","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-thm-hopkins.md","title":"Hopkins–Levitzki Theorem","display":"thm-hopkins — Hopkins–Levitzki Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-hopkins","aliases":["58-thm-hopkins"],"display":"thm-hopkins — Hopkins–Levitzki Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-df-artinian.md]]","[[../batch11/58-df-ring.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-powerset.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-hopkins"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-hopkins</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-hopkins — Hopkins–Levitzki Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"0ad886c6bc35a838\" href=\"?note=0ad886c6bc35a838\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-artinian.md\">../batch02/58-df-artinian.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"1c30d21ea7b443f6\" href=\"?note=1c30d21ea7b443f6\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-ring.md\">../batch11/58-df-ring.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2b6b1d9eb78a2714\" href=\"?note=2b6b1d9eb78a2714\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-powerset.md\">../batch09/58-df-powerset.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R,I\\in V\">\\(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R,I\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ring}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\operatorname{Ring}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"1c30d21ea7b443f6\" href=\"?note=1c30d21ea7b443f6\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-ring.md\">../batch11/58-df-ring.md</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"0ad886c6bc35a838\" href=\"?note=0ad886c6bc35a838\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-artinian.md\">../batch02/58-df-artinian.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P:V\\to V\">\\(\\mathcal P:V\\to V\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"2b6b1d9eb78a2714\" href=\"?note=2b6b1d9eb78a2714\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-powerset.md\">../batch09/58-df-powerset.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S,\\mathrm{LeftNoetherian}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S,\\mathrm{LeftNoetherian}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span> are defined below.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}left\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}for\\text{-}hopkins}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S(I,R,+,\\cdot,0_R)\\leftrightarrow\nI\\subseteq R\\land0_R\\in I\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in I\\;(x+y\\in I)\\land\n\\forall x\\in I\\;\\exists y\\in I\\;(x+y=0_R\\land y+x=0_R)\\land\n\\forall r\\in R\\;\\forall x\\in I\\;(r\\cdot x\\in I)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}left\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}for\\text{-}hopkins}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S(I,R,+,\\cdot,0_R)\\leftrightarrow\nI\\subseteq R\\land0_R\\in I\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in I\\;(x+y\\in I)\\land\n\\forall x\\in I\\;\\exists y\\in I\\;(x+y=0_R\\land y+x=0_R)\\land\n\\forall r\\in R\\;\\forall x\\in I\\;(r\\cdot x\\in I)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}left\\text{-}noetherian\\text{-}for\\text{-}hopkins}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LeftNoetherian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\land\n\\forall J\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(J,\\omega,\\mathcal P(R))\\land\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S(J(n),R,+,\\cdot,0_R)\\land J(n)\\subseteq J(n+1)\\bigr)\n\\to\\exists N\\in\\omega\\;\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(N\\leq n\\to J(n)=J(N))\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}left\\text{-}noetherian\\text{-}for\\text{-}hopkins}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LeftNoetherian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\land\n\\forall J\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(J,\\omega,\\mathcal P(R))\\land\n\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{LeftIdeal}_S(J(n),R,+,\\cdot,0_R)\\land J(n)\\subseteq J(n+1)\\bigr)\n\\to\\exists N\\in\\omega\\;\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(N\\leq n\\to J(n)=J(N))\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}hopkins}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\n\\to\\mathrm{LeftNoetherian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}hopkins}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\n\\to\\mathrm{LeftNoetherian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The right-handed analogue is obtained separately by applying the theorem to the opposite ring.</li>\n<li>For unital rings, the left Artinian condition implies the left Noetherian condition; the converse fails in general.</li>\n<li>Left Artinian does not by itself assert right Artinian in the noncommutative setting.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-df-artinian.md","status":"resolved","id":"0ad886c6bc35a838","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-artinian.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch11/58-df-ring.md","status":"resolved","id":"1c30d21ea7b443f6","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-ring.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-powerset.md","status":"resolved","id":"2b6b1d9eb78a2714","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-powerset.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch11/58-df-ring.md","status":"resolved","id":"1c30d21ea7b443f6","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Ring}_S\\subseteq V^5$ and $\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S\\subseteq V^5$ (see [[../batch11/58-df-ring.md]], [[../batch02/58-df-artinian.md]]).","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-artinian.md","status":"resolved","id":"0ad886c6bc35a838","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Ring}_S\\subseteq V^5$ and $\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S\\subseteq V^5$ (see [[../batch11/58-df-ring.md]], [[../batch02/58-df-artinian.md]]).","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved